AVC-Reward integration notice

Ayase contains an independently authored runtime wrapper for AVC-Reward. It does
not redistribute the AVC-Reward source code, prompt, or model weights. At runtime,
the wrapper downloads the pinned author-served protocol file from:

https://github.com/Tsuki0512/AVC-Reward/tree/eb0659862ff6888dcc8e92e3bf69c7590d59d54d

and the trained checkpoint from:

https://huggingface.co/Tsuki0512/AVC-Reward/tree/84dd3998ecc6070925f08dca37132a424e667a52

The upstream project states "Research use only." The Hugging Face checkpoint is
tagged license "other" and supplies no more specific model-license text. Those
terms apply to the downloaded assets; Ayase's MIT license does not replace them.


Frame selection follows the independently reproduced OpenCV defaults in vLLM
v0.12.0 (Apache-2.0): https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/v0.12.0/vllm/multimodal/video.py
